<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Tools — the Orpheus environment</title>
<style>
  :root { --paper:#fbf8f3; --rule:#8e8a7a; --title:#cfcaba; --ink:#1a1320; --accent:#5a1530; --heart:#8a1538; }
  body { font-family:'Ligos', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; max-width:48rem; margin:3rem auto; padding:0 1rem; line-height:1.6; color:var(--ink); background:var(--paper); }
  h1 { font-variant:small-caps; letter-spacing:.03em; color:var(--accent); font-size:2.4rem; margin-bottom:0; }
  .sub { color:#8a6d3b; font-style:italic; margin:.2rem 0 1.6rem; }
  .panel { background:var(--paper); border:1.5px solid var(--rule); border-radius:4px; margin:1.4rem 0; box-shadow:0 1px 4px #0001; }
  .panel > .t { background:var(--title); border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--rule); padding:5px 11px; font-weight:700; font-variant:small-caps; letter-spacing:.04em; color:var(--accent); border-radius:4px 4px 0 0; }
  .panel > .t .sig { float:right; font-weight:400; font-style:italic; color:#7a6d3b; font-size:.85rem; }
  .panel > .b { padding:11px 13px; }
  .lede { margin:.1rem 0 .8rem; color:#473b4a; }
  table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:.4rem 0; }
  td, th { border-bottom:1px solid #e4dccc; padding:.32rem .6rem; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; }
  th { color:var(--accent); font-variant:small-caps; letter-spacing:.03em; }
  code { background:#efe9dd; padding:0 .3rem; border-radius:3px; font-family:'DejaVu Sans Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; font-size:.92em; }
  .out { color:var(--heart); font-weight:700; }
  .feat { color:#6b6256; font-style:italic; font-size:.9em; }
  .tool { margin:.55rem 0; padding:.45rem .6rem; border:1px solid #ece2cc; border-radius:5px; background:#fffdf8; }
  .tool .lbl { font-size:.9rem; color:#6b6256; margin-bottom:.32rem; }
  .tool .lbl code { color:var(--accent); }
  .live { display:inline-flex; gap:.4rem; align-items:baseline; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  .live input.li, .live select.li { font-family:inherit; font-size:.95rem; padding:.2rem .45rem; border:1px solid var(--rule); border-radius:3px; background:#fff; color:var(--ink); }
  .live input[type=range].li { padding:0; vertical-align:middle; accent-color:var(--accent); }
  .live .liv { font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; color:var(--accent); min-width:2.4em; display:inline-block; font-size:.9rem; }
  .live .out svg { max-width:100%; height:auto; vertical-align:middle; margin-top:.3rem; border:1px solid #e4dccc; border-radius:3px; }
  .tool .out svg { max-width:100%; height:auto; }
  footer { margin-top:2.4rem; color:#998; font-size:.85rem; border-top:1px solid #e4dccc; padding-top:1rem; }
</style>

<h1>Environment Tools</h1>
<p class="sub">Every module the environment exposes, each in its own frame — every tool a live, interactive interface.</p>

<p class="lede">A <b>Facet</b> page is pure markup whose holes call environment tools with the Oberon
convention <code>Module.procedure(args)</code>. For guided, tutorial-style versions of these
tools — algorithms animated a step at a time, the language taught in live boxes — see
<a href="/learn"><b>the Learn page</b></a>. Every tool below is a <b>live widget</b>: type in a
field and the result updates as you go, re-evaluated on the server through <code>/api/eval</code>
(debounced and cached on both sides). With JavaScript off, each widget still shows its
server-rendered default — so the page reads correctly either way and stays byte-for-byte
deterministic per request.</p>

<!-- ===================== Meta ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Meta — the catalogue, live <span class="sig">modules · tools · count</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">This page is self-describing: <code>Meta.count()</code> &rarr;
    <span class="out">{{ Meta.count() }}</span>. The full module list,
    <code>Meta.modules()</code> &rarr; <span class="out">{{ Meta.modules() }}</span>.</p>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Meta.tools(module)</code> — pick a module to list everything it exposes</div>
      {{ Live.box("Meta.tools(module)", [["module", "Mkt", "SCArs", "Phono", "Txt", "Latte", "Viz", "Mkt", "Date", "Sent", "Hash", "Live", "Meta"]]) }}
    </div>
    <p class="feat">These read the same registries that drive every frame below, so the catalogue
    can't drift from what's actually callable — the tools-page test enforces exactly that.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== SCArs ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">SCArs — the sound-change applier <span class="sig">pie · evolve · apply · trace</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">The historical pipeline runs <b>PIE</b> &rarr;<code>pie</code>&rarr; <b>Solar
    Speech</b> &rarr;<code>evolve</code>&rarr; <b>Heart Speech</b>. Run either leg live, then apply
    or trace your own ordered rule sets.</p>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>SCArs.pie(word)</code> — Proto-Indo-European &rarr; Solar Speech</div>
      {{ Live.box("SCArs.pie(word)", ["word", "nokʷt"]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>SCArs.evolve(word)</code> — Solar Speech &rarr; modern Heart Speech</div>
      {{ Live.box("SCArs.evolve(word)", ["word", "ligā"]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>SCArs.apply(word, rule…)</code> — apply your own rules (separate with <code>;</code>)</div>
      {{ Live.box("SCArs.apply(word, Txt.split(rules, \";\"))", ["word", "kasa", "rules", "k>g; a>o"]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>SCArs.trace(word, rule…)</code> — show the derivation after each rule</div>
      {{ Live.box("SCArs.trace(word, Txt.split(rules, \";\"))", ["word", "kasa", "rules", "k>g; a>o"]) }}
    </div>

    <p class="feat" style="margin-top:.7rem">Rule grammar for <code>apply</code> and <code>trace</code>:
    substitution <code>k&gt;g</code>, environment <code>s&gt;z/a_a</code>, deletion
    <code>h&gt;</code>, clusters <code>ps&gt;f</code>, word boundaries <code>#</code>, and
    metathesis. Chain as many as you like, applied in order.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Phono ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Phono — phonology <span class="sig">presets · inventory · words · report · coin</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">Generate plausible vocabulary from a sound system. Pick a built-in preset or
    define your own inventory; words are coined deterministically from a seed, so the same choices
    always give the same list. Built-in presets: <code>Phono.presets()</code> &rarr;
    <span class="out">{{ Phono.presets() }}</span></p>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Phono.inventory(preset)</code> — the chosen preset's sounds and syllable shapes</div>
      {{ Live.box("Phono.inventory(preset)", [["preset", "polynesian", "polynesian", "pie", "semitic", "sinitic"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Phono.words(preset, n, seed)</code> — coin words from a preset (change the seed for a new batch)</div>
      {{ Live.box("Phono.words(preset, n, seed)", [["preset", "polynesian", "polynesian", "pie", "semitic", "sinitic"], ["n", "10", "~", "1", "40", "1"], ["seed", "7"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Phono.report(preset)</code> — a typological sanity check against cross-linguistic norms</div>
      {{ Live.box("Phono.report(preset)", [["preset", "semitic", "polynesian", "pie", "semitic", "sinitic"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Phono.coin(consonants, vowels, patterns, n, seed)</code> — coin from your <em>own</em> inventory
      (space-separated; patterns use <code>C</code> and <code>V</code>)</div>
      {{ Live.box("Phono.coin(consonants, vowels, patterns, n, seed)", [["consonants", "p t k m n l s w"], ["vowels", "a e i o u"], ["patterns", "CV CVC CCV"], ["n", "10"], ["seed", "3"]]) }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Txt ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Txt — composable text helpers <span class="sig">11 string operations</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">A complete little text toolkit; every operation is live. List results render as
    <code>[a b c]</code>.</p>

    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.upper(s)</code> — upper-case</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.upper(s)", ["s", "heart speech"]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.lower(s)</code> — lower-case</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.lower(s)", ["s", "HEART SPEECH"]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.cap(s)</code> — capitalize the first character</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.cap(s)", ["s", "heardō"]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.rev(s)</code> — reverse the characters</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.rev(s)", ["s", "solar"]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.trim(s)</code> — strip surrounding whitespace</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.trim(s)", ["s", "  spaced  "]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.len(s)</code> — character count</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.len(s)", ["s", "heardō"]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.words(s)</code> — split into a list of words</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.words(s)", ["s", "heart of speech"]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.replace(s, from, to)</code> — replace every occurrence</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.replace(s, from, to)", ["s", "banana", "from", "a", "to", "o"]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.split(s, sep)</code> — split into a list on a separator</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.split(s, sep)", ["s", "k>g; a>o", "sep", ";"]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.join(list, sep)</code> — join a list; pick the separator</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.join(Txt.split(items, \",\"), sep)", [["items", "sol, luna, stella"], ["sep", " · ", " · ", ", ", " | ", " — ", ""]]) }}</div>
    <div class="tool"><div class="lbl"><code>Txt.esc(s)</code> — HTML-escape user input</div>
      {{ Live.box("Txt.esc(s)", ["s", "<tag> & co"]) }}</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Latte ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Latte — the language, evaluated live <span class="sig">eval(expr)</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">Type any Latte expression — arithmetic, lists, higher-order functions,
    recursion — and it runs on Loom (fuel-bounded, side-effect-free) as you type.</p>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Latte.eval(expr)</code> — evaluate a Latte expression and render the result</div>
      {{ Live.box("Latte.eval(expr)", ["expr", "(map (fn [x] -> (mul x x)) (range 6))"]) }}
    </div>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Latte.eval(expr)</code> — or pick a worked example from the dropdown</div>
      {{ Live.box("Latte.eval(expr)", [["expr", "(range 5)", "(range 5)", "(map (fn [x] -> (mul x x)) (range 6))", "(filter (fn [x] -> (gt x 2)) (range 6))", "(foldl (fn [a v] -> (add a v)) 0 (range 10))", "(reverse (range 5))"]]) }}
    </div>

    <p class="feat" style="margin-top:.6rem">Things to try by editing the field above:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Expression</th><th>Feature</th></tr>
      <tr><td><code>(foldl (fn [a v] -> (add a v)) 0 (range 10))</code></td><td class="feat">fold to a scalar</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>(filter (fn [x] -> (gt x 2)) (range 6))</code></td><td class="feat">higher-order filter</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>(reverse (range 5))</code></td><td class="feat">list reversal</td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Viz ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Viz — charts <span class="sig">chart(kind, numbers)</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">Turn a list of numbers into an SVG chart. Because a Facet hole emits markup
    directly, the chart is drawn right into the page — and with <code>Live.view</code> it redraws as
    you type. Enter numbers (space- or comma-separated) and choose a chart kind:</p>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Viz.chart(kind, numbers)</code> — bars, line, or scatter</div>
      {{ Live.view("Viz.chart(kind, numbers)", [["kind", "bars", "bars", "line", "scatter"], ["numbers", "5 9 7 12 8 15 11 18 14 22 19 25"]]) }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Trade ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Trade — the advisor, switchable between markets live</div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">The full advisory report — the very function the CLI prints (<code>latte
    trade</code>): US Treasuries route to the duration model (69.6% out-of-sample edge, named
    factor drivers), any price tape to the TA/volatility/news engine. Pick a market; the
    report re-runs.</p>
    {{ Live.view("Trade.advice(market, 10000)", [["market", "bonds", "bonds", "btc", "eth", "ltc", "xrp", "ada", "doge", "sol"]]) }}
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Mkt ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Mkt — market-data lab <span class="sig">span · stat · series · chart · vol · advice</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">A read-only, deterministic lab over the built-in BTC/USD daily close series — one
    place to <b>query</b> the data, <b>chart</b> it, and run the <b>quantitative signals</b> the
    trading advisor is built on. Coverage: <code>Mkt.span()</code> &rarr;
    <span class="out">{{ Mkt.span() }}</span></p>

    <p class="feat" style="margin-top:.5rem">Query &amp; aggregate (the database role):</p>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Mkt.stat(op)</code> — aggregate the whole series</div>
      {{ Live.box("Mkt.stat(op)", [["op", "last", "last", "first", "min", "max", "mean", "range", "count"]]) }}
    </div>

    <p class="feat" style="margin-top:.6rem">Visualize (the chart pipes <code>Mkt.series(n)</code> straight into <code>Viz.chart</code>):</p>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Viz.chart(kind, Mkt.series(n))</code> — chart the last n closes, live</div>
      {{ Live.view("Viz.chart(kind, Mkt.series(n))", [["kind", "line", "line", "bars", "scatter"], ["n", "90", "~", "2", "1318", "1"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Mkt.chart(kind, n)</code> — the same chart as a single tool call</div>
      {{ Live.view("Mkt.chart(kind, n)", [["kind", "bars", "bars", "line", "scatter"], ["n", "60", "~", "2", "1318", "1"]]) }}
    </div>

    <p class="feat" style="margin-top:.6rem">Analyze (the trading advisor's fast signal layer) — drag the window:</p>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Mkt.vol(window)</code> — realized volatility over the last <em>window</em> days</div>
      {{ Live.box("Mkt.vol(window)", [["window", "30", "~", "2", "1318", "1"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Mkt.advice(window)</code> — momentum vs a moving average → a direction</div>
      {{ Live.box("Mkt.advice(window)", [["window", "10", "~", "2", "1317", "1"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Mkt.series(n)</code> — the raw last-n closes (what the chart is drawn from)</div>
      {{ Live.box("Mkt.series(n)", [["n", "12", "~", "2", "1318", "1"]]) }}
    </div>
    <p class="feat" style="margin-top:.5rem">The volatility model the advisor reports —
    <code>Mkt.forecast()</code> &rarr; <span class="out">{{ Mkt.forecast() }}</span></p>

    <p class="feat" style="margin-top:.6rem">The deep model — a logistic-regression volatility-regime
    classifier trained in Latte — takes several seconds per run, so it stays a command-line tool
    (<code>latte fin</code>) rather than a live widget; everything above responds instantly.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Date ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Date — civil date arithmetic <span class="sig">add · between · weekday · ordinal · fromordinal</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">Calendar math on <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> dates, with no clock involved — purely a
    function of the inputs, so it stays deterministic. Drag the day offset or edit the dates:</p>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Date.add(date, days)</code> — shift a date by whole days</div>
      {{ Live.box("Date.add(date, days)", [["date", "2026-06-10"], ["days", "7", "~", "-3650", "3650", "1"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Date.between(a, b)</code> — days from one date to another</div>
      {{ Live.box("Date.between(a, b)", [["a", "2022-11-01"], ["b", "2026-06-10"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Date.weekday(date)</code> — the day of the week</div>
      {{ Live.box("Date.weekday(date)", [["date", "2026-06-10"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Date.ordinal(date)</code> — day number since 1970-01-01</div>
      {{ Live.box("Date.ordinal(date)", [["date", "2026-06-10"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Date.fromordinal(n)</code> — the inverse: a day number back to a date</div>
      {{ Live.box("Date.fromordinal(n)", [["n", "20614", "~", "-25000", "25000", "1"]]) }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Sent ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Sent — text sentiment <span class="sig">polarity · label · counts</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">Score the sentiment of free text — a lexicon fused with a model, the same signal
    the trading advisor folds in from news. Type and watch it update:</p>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Sent.label(text)</code> — positive, negative, or neutral, with the score</div>
      {{ Live.box("Sent.label(text)", [["text", "a wonderful and great result"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Sent.polarity(text)</code> — the raw polarity in [-1, 1]</div>
      {{ Live.box("Sent.polarity(text)", [["text", "a wonderful and great result"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Sent.counts(text)</code> — how many positive and negative words it found</div>
      {{ Live.box("Sent.counts(text)", [["text", "good news but also some bad risk"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="w">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Sent.bond(text)</code> — the same engine read for BOND prices: the
      hawkish/dovish policy axis, with risk-off scored as a Treasury bid. "Hot inflation forces
      aggressive hikes" is bullish for nothing — except it is bearish for bonds specifically,
      while a plain disaster headline is a bond bid.</div>
      {{ Live.box("Sent.bond(text)", [["text", "hot inflation forces aggressive hikes"]]) }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== AlgoViz ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">AlgoViz — algorithms, played <span class="sig">frame · steps</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="feat">The <code>algoviz</code> library instruments classic algorithms: every
    comparison, swap, probe, and visit appends a frame to a trace, and a frame renders through
    the same <code>gfx</code> scene pipeline <code>latte gfx</code> draws. Drag <code>k</code>
    and the algorithm runs, step by step, on Loom. The <a href="/learn">Learn page</a> builds
    full tutorials around these.</p>
    <div class="w">
      <div class="lbl"><code>AlgoViz.frame(algo, xs, k, t)</code> — step k of bubble, insert,
      binsearch, or bfs over the list xs (t is the binsearch target)</div>
      {{ Live.view("AlgoViz.frame(algo, xs, k, t)", [["algo", "bubble", "bubble", "insert", "quick", "binsearch", "bfs"], ["xs", "5 2 8 1 9 3"], ["k", "0", "~", "0", "40", "1"], ["t", "8", "~", "0", "12", "1"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="w">
      <div class="lbl"><code>AlgoViz.steps(algo, xs, t)</code> — how many frames the trace has
      (the slider's true range)</div>
      {{ Live.box("AlgoViz.steps(algo, xs, t)", [["algo", "bubble", "bubble", "insert", "quick", "binsearch", "bfs"], ["xs", "5 2 8 1 9 3"], ["t", "8"]]) }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Hash ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Hash — digests <span class="sig">sha3 · short</span></div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">SHA3-256 over any text — deterministic, and the digest changes completely with
    the smallest edit. Type to watch it churn:</p>

    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Hash.sha3(text)</code> — the full 64-hex digest</div>
      {{ Live.box("Hash.sha3(text)", [["text", "Orpheus"]]) }}
    </div>
    <div class="tool">
      <div class="lbl"><code>Hash.short(text, n)</code> — a short fingerprint of n hex characters</div>
      {{ Live.box("Hash.short(text, n)", [["text", "Orpheus"], ["n", "12", "~", "1", "64", "1"]]) }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Db ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Db — shared persistent state (the <a href="/board">Board</a> lives on these)</div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">The write-ahead-logged database, as page widgets: post (Lamport-pair key),
    list (newest first), and reconcile with a peer node (G-Set union). Side-effecting tools
    sit in <code>Live.form</code> — they run only when clicked.</p>
    {{ Live.form("Db.post(\"board\", author, text)", [["author", "anon"], ["text", "hello from the tools page"]]) }}
    {{ Live.view("Db.board(\"board\", n)", [["n", "5", "~", "3", "30", "1"]]) }}
    {{ Live.form("Db.sync(\"board\", url)", [["url", "http://127.0.0.1:8089"]]) }}
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ===================== Kv ===================== -->
<div class="panel">
  <div class="t">Kv — the ledger: event-sourced, gossiped state (the <a href="/network">Network</a> page lives on these)</div>
  <div class="b">
    <p class="lede">The GUI hosts a persistent kv <b>node</b> (the same machinery <code>latte node</code>
    runs): every <code>Kv.put</code> is a durable event in an append-only log, gossiped to every
    connected peer; state is the deterministic fold of that log, so connected instances converge
    byte-for-byte — and every past state is one <code>Kv.at</code> away. Side-effecting tools sit in
    <code>Live.form</code>.</p>
    {{ Live.view("Kv.info()", [["_", "0"]]) }}
    {{ Live.form("Kv.put(key, value)", [["key", "greeting"], ["value", "hello, network"]]) }}
    {{ Live.form("Kv.del(key)", [["key", "greeting"]]) }}
    {{ Live.watch("Kv.state()", [], 4) }}
